  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material implying generational amnesia",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'only 30's kids will remember this', which implicitly addresses the viewer as someone who may not belong to the generation that remembers the Holocaust, thereby positioning the user as part of a younger generation potentially disconnected from this historical memory. This projection is not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me'), but is inferred through the rhetorical framing of the text, which creates a sense of shared identity with the viewer as someone who might not remember or care about the event depicted.",
